// Title: EventLog EVTX File Deleted
// Sigma ID: 63c779ba-f638-40a0-a593-ddd45e8b1ddc
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-02-15 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1070
// Description: Detects the deletion of the event log files which may indicate an attempt to destroy forensic
//   evidence
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - Internal Research
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/file/file_delete/file_delete_win_delete_event_log_files.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where ActionType =~ "FileDeleted" and (FolderPath startswith "C:\\Windows\\System32\\winevt\\Logs\\" and FolderPath endswith ".evtx")
